What we’ve created

OBSERVE

Collect evidence and identify the frame

DECOMPOSE & INFER

Recover structures, operators, and candidate mechanisms

RECONSTRUCT & PREDICT

Generate behavior using a forward model

COMPARE & REVISE

Measure discrepancies and refine the mechanism

Repeat until adequately validated

TRANSFER

Rebuild the validated function in another domain

The module includes an eight-stage investigative process, a structured evidence ledger, an operator grammar, multi-domain adapters, a JSON example, validation tests, and instructions that another AI can use to reconstruct the architecture.

Its distinction from REA is important. REA provides software-inspection tooling and evidence-bearing results; ARKFORGE is our proposed generalized reasoning and reconstruction layer.

How to activate it

